{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421569802,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_LnXorsIGoW10y2o20pHd3129","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review"},"output":"     500 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\n    2506 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n     471 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md\n      97 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n     218 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n     492 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n    4284 total\n","metadata":{"output":"     500 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\n    2506 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n     471 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md\n      97 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n     218 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n     492 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n    4284 total\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"wc -l .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml","time":{"start":1792421569777,"end":1792421569801}},"id":"prt_154a6a315001BBCyBBVuPCnipy","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a68de1001w9pA0IkGp81G17"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421569987,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_SMUBh6NybpY4kaV88gqN6974","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Log Records\n3: description: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n6:   - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n7:   - \"review depth schema\"\n8:   - \"review traceability checks\"\n9:   - \"review graph events\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.0.6\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Log Records\n16: \n17: The `deep-review-state.jsonl` log is the append-only source of truth for a review run. This reference documents the config, iteration, event, and lineage record schemas plus the Review Depth Schema (v2) that the reducer consumes.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: This reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n30: - Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n31: - Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n32: - Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n33: \n34: ### Key Sources\n35: \n36: | Source | Purpose |\n37: |--------|---------|\n38: | Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n39: | Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n40: | Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n41: | Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n46: \n47: Append-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n48: \n49: While the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n50: \n51: ### Line 1: Config Record\n52: \n53: ```json\n54: {\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n58: \n59: ### Iteration Records\n60: \n61: ```json\n62: {\n63:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n64:   \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n65:   \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n66:   \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n67:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n68:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n69:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n70:   \"generation\": 1,\n71:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n72:   \"findingsCount\": 4,\n73:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n74:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n75:   \"findingDetails\": [\n76:     {\n77:       \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n78:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n79:       \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n80:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n81:       \"file\": \"path/to/file.ts:42\",\n82:       \"evidence\": \"Observed consumer still reads the old field.\",\n83:       \"recommendation\": \"Update the consumer and add verification.\",\n84:       \"disposition\": \"active\",\n85:       \"findingClass\": \"cross-consumer\",\n86:       \"scopeProof\": \"rg evidence covering producers and consumers\",\n87:       \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"producer/helper\", \"consumer/status\"]\n88:     }\n89:   ],\n90:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.32,\n91:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T14:30:00Z\", \"durationMs\": 52000\n92: }\n93: ```\n94: \n95: **Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n96: \n97: **Legacy field:** `run`, the older name for `iteration`. Readers still accept it and the fan-out stop-policy validator does not; new records write `iteration`. Event records keep their own `run` field.\n98: \n99: **Optional fields:** `parentSessionId`, `continuedFromRun`, `findingsRefined`, `findingRefs`, `traceabilityChecks`, `coverage`, `noveltyJustification`, `ruledOut`, `focusTrack`, `scoreEstimate`, `segment`, `convergenceSignals`, `graphEvents`\n100: \n101: | Required Field | Type | Description |\n102: |---------------|------|-------------|\n103: | mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n104: | dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n105: | filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n106: | sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n107: | generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n108: | lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n109: | findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n110: | findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n111: | findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n112: | newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n113: \n114: ### Convergence Signals\n115: \n116: | Signal | Weight | Description |\n117: |--------|--------|-------------|\n118: | rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n119: | madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n120: | dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n121: | compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n122: \n123: **Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n124: \n125: ### Graph Events\n126: \n127: The optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The MCP coverage graph handlers (`mcp-server/handlers/coverage-graph/upsert.ts`) consume these events and persist them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n128: \n129: ```json\n130: {\n131:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n132:   \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n133:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n134:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n135:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n136:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n137:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n138:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n139:   \"generation\": 1,\n140:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n141:   \"graphEvents\": [\n142:     { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n143:     { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n144:     { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n145:     { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n146:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n147:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n148:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n151:   \"durationMs\": 51000\n152: }\n153: ```\n154: \n155: #### Event payload shape\n156: \n157: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n158: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n159: | type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n160: | id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n161: | label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n162: | relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n163: | source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n164: | target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n165: | metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n166: \n167: #### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n168: \n169: `graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n170: \n171: Concrete obligations for producers:\n172: \n173: 1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n174: 2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n175: 3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n176: 4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n177: \n178: The collision regression in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/session-isolation.vitest.ts` (\"shared-ID collisions\" block) exercises this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows must survive independently.\n179: \n180: ### Synthesis Event\n181: \n182: ```json\n183: {\n184:   \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n185:   \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n186:   \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n187:   \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n188:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n189: }\n190: ```\n191: \n192: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n193: \n194: ### Blocked-Stop Event\n195: \n196: When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n197: \n198: ```json\n199: {\n200:   \"type\": \"event\",\n201:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n202:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n203:   \"run\": 4,\n204:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n205:   \"gateResults\": {\n206:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n207:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n208:       \"pass\": false,\n209:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n210:       \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n211:     },\n212:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n213:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n214:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n215:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n216:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n217:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n218:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n219:   },\n220:   \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Cover the missing review dimensions, then resolve the active P0.\",\n221:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:45:00Z\",\n222:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n223:   \"generation\": 1\n224: }\n225: ```\n226: \n227: `gateResults` carries the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`: `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. The last two are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. See `../convergence/convergence.md` §Section-1 for the authoritative shape.\n228: \n229: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n230: \n231: ### Graph Convergence Event\n232: \n233: Before the inline 3-signal review vote is allowed to finalize STOP, the workflow must append a `graph_convergence` event for the current review lineage.\n234: \n235: ```json\n236: {\n237:   \"type\": \"event\",\n238:   \"event\": \"graph_convergence\",\n239:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n240:   \"run\": 4,\n241:   \"decision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n242:   \"signals\": {\n243:     \"dimensionCoverage\": 1,\n244:     \"findingStability\": 0.88,\n245:     \"p0ResolutionRate\": 1,\n246:     \"evidenceDensity\": 1.4,\n247:     \"hotspotSaturation\": 0.75\n248:   },\n249:   \"blockers\": [],\n250:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:44:00Z\",\n251:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n252:   \"generation\": 1\n253: }\n254: ```\n255: \n256: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `decision`, `signals`, `blockers`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n257: \n258: **Decision enum:** `CONTINUE`, `STOP_ALLOWED`, `STOP_BLOCKED`\n259: \n260: **Combined-stop rule:** Final STOP is legal only when the inline review convergence decision says STOP and the latest `graph_convergence.decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\"`. If the latest graph decision is `STOP_BLOCKED`, set `stop_blocked=true`, emit `blocked_stop`, and continue recovery instead of stopping. If the latest graph decision is `CONTINUE`, downgrade the inline STOP candidate to CONTINUE.\n261: \n262: ### Normalized Pause and Recovery Events\n263: \n264: Pause and recovery events MUST use the frozen shared stop-reason enum at emission time:\n265: \n266: `converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`\n267: \n268: Raw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` labels are not legal persisted event names in the review JSONL contract. The workflow must rewrite them before appending JSONL rows.\n269: \n270: ```json\n271: {\n272:   \"type\": \"event\",\n273:   \"event\": \"userPaused\",\n274:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n275:   \"stopReason\": \"userPaused\",\n276:   \"reason\": \"sentinel file detected\",\n277:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:32:00Z\",\n278:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n279:   \"generation\": 1\n280: }\n281: ```\n282: \n283: ```json\n284: {\n285:   \"type\": \"event\",\n286:   \"event\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n287:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n288:   \"stopReason\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n289:   \"fromIteration\": 5,\n290:   \"strategy\": \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\",\n291:   \"targetDimension\": \"traceability\",\n292:   \"outcome\": \"pending\",\n293:   \"reason\": \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\",\n294:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:40:00Z\",\n295:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n296:   \"generation\": 1\n297: }\n298: ```\n299: \n300: **Emission rule:** If runtime logic first identifies a raw `paused` or `stuck_recovery` condition, the workflow MUST normalize it to `userPaused` or `stuckRecovery` before writing the JSONL line. Reducers and dashboards may assume persisted event names are already normalized.\n301: \n302: ### Verdict Rules\n303: \n304: | Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n305: |---------|-----------|--------------|\n306: | FAIL | `activeP0 > 0` OR quality gate failure | `/speckit:plan` |\n307: | CONDITIONAL | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 > 0` | `/speckit:plan` |\n308: | PASS | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` | `/create:changelog` |\n309: \n310: When `activeP2 > 0` on PASS, set `hasAdvisories: true`.\n311: \n312: ### traceabilityChecks Schema\n313: \n314: ```json\n315: {\n316:   \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n317:     \"summary\": {\n318:       \"required\": 2, \"executed\": 3, \"pass\": 1, \"partial\": 1,\n319:       \"fail\": 1, \"blocked\": 0, \"notApplicable\": 0, \"gatingFailures\": 1\n320:     },\n321:     \"results\": [{\n322:       \"protocolId\": \"spec_code\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n323:       \"applicable\": true, \"counts\": { \"pass\": 0, \"partial\": 0, \"fail\": 1 },\n324:       \"evidence\": [\"README.md:48\"], \"findingRefs\": [\"F004\"],\n325:       \"summary\": \"README claimed the old report contract.\"\n326:     }]\n327:   }\n328: }\n329: ```\n330: \n331: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n332: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n333: | summary.required / executed / pass / partial / fail / blocked / notApplicable | number | Yes | Protocol execution counts |\n334: | summary.gatingFailures | number | Yes | Hard-gate failures blocking STOP |\n335: | results[].protocolId | string | Yes | Canonical protocol identifier |\n336: | results[].status | string | Yes | `pass`, `partial`, `fail`, `blocked`, `notApplicable` |\n337: | results[].gateClass | string | Yes | `hard` or `advisory` |\n338: | results[].applicable | boolean | Yes | Whether the protocol applied |\n339: | results[].counts | object | Yes | Protocol-local summary counts |\n340: | results[].evidence | string[] | No | Supporting file:line refs |\n341: | results[].findingRefs | string[] | No | Related finding identifiers |\n342: | results[].summary | string | Yes | Human-readable one-line result |\n343: \n344: ### Validation Rules\n345: \n346: - Each line must be valid JSON with a `type` field\n347: - `mode` must be `\"review\"` on all iteration and synthesis records\n348: - `iteration` values must be sequential. `newFindingsRatio` must be 0.0-1.0\n349: - `findingsSummary` and `findingsNew` must each contain `P0`, `P1`, `P2` keys\n350: - `findingDetails` must be an array. Each active item must include `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`\n351: \n352: ---\n353: \n354: ## 3. REVIEW DEPTH SCHEMA (V2)\n355: \n356: `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2` is the discriminator for the v2 search-depth contract. Absent values, `null`, or any value other than `2` mean v1 legacy: readers keep today's behavior, and validator hard enforcement applies only when the discriminator is present.\n357: \n358: Frozen v2 contract:\n359: \n360: Top-level review iteration fields when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`:\n361: - `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`, discriminator\n362: - `reviewDepthApplicability`, `{ scopeClass: 'trivial'|'standard'|'complex', enforcement: 'strict'|'warn'|'skip', reason: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n363: - `targetSelection`, `{ selectedTargets: string[], selectionReason: string, discoveryMethods: string[], omittedHighRiskTargets: string[], graphStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', semanticSearchStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n364: - `searchCoverage`, `{ requiredBugClasses: string[], covered: string[], ruledOut: string[], deferred: string[], blocked: string[], graphCoverageMode: 'graph'|'graphless_fallback'|'unavailable_blocked' }`\n365: - `searchLedger[]`, array of ledger rows\n366: \n367: Ledger row fields:\n368: - Required: `id, dimension, targetRefs, bugClass, disposition, rationale`\n369: - `hypothesis` (string) OR `invariant` (string), at least one\n370: - `searchActions[]`, `{ method: string, queryOrPath: string, result: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n371: - Disposition-specific link (exactly one):\n372:   - `finding` → `linkedFindingId` (must reference an id present in `findingDetails[]`)\n373:   - `ruled_out` → `ruledOutReason`\n374:   - `deferred` → `deferredReason`\n375:   - `blocked` → `blockedReason`\n376:   - `not_applicable` → `notApplicableReason`\n377: \n378: Trivial-scope exemption: when `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass === 'trivial'` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.enforcement === 'skip'`, ledger may be `[]` with cited scope proof in `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`.\n379: \n380: ### Applicability\n381: \n382: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n383: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n384: | `scopeClass` | `'trivial' \\| 'standard' \\| 'complex'` | Yes | Classifies how much depth proof the review target warrants. |\n385: | `enforcement` | `'strict' \\| 'warn' \\| 'skip'` | Yes | `strict` means v2 validators fail shallow records, `warn` emits advisory rollout feedback, `skip` is valid only for trivial scope with proof. |\n386: | `reason` | string | Yes | Human-readable justification for the chosen scope/enforcement pair. |\n387: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | File/path refs proving scope classification, required even for skipped trivial ledgers. |\n388: \n389: ### Target Selection\n390: \n391: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n392: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n393: | `selectedTargets` | string[] | Yes | Files, folders, specs, or surfaces actually searched this iteration. |\n394: | `selectionReason` | string | Yes | Why these targets were highest-value for the dimension or bug class. |\n395: | `discoveryMethods` | string[] | Yes | Methods such as direct read, exact search, semantic search, graph query, producer trace, consumer trace, or negative-test search. |\n396: | `omittedHighRiskTargets` | string[] | Yes | High-risk targets not searched, use `[]` when none were identified. |\n397: | `graphStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Code/coverage graph availability for this iteration's target selection. |\n398: | `semanticSearchStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Semantic/code search availability for this iteration. |\n399: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | Evidence for target selection and omitted-target claims. |\n400: \n401: ### Search Coverage\n402: \n403: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n404: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n405: | `requiredBugClasses` | string[] | Yes | Bug classes or invariant families that should be searched for this scope. |\n406: | `covered` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched with conclusive finding or clean proof. |\n407: | `ruledOut` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched and explicitly ruled out. |\n408: | `deferred` | string[] | Yes | Required classes postponed with a reason in ledger rows. |\n409: | `blocked` | string[] | Yes | Required classes blocked by missing access, graph/search outage, ambiguity, or scope conflict. |\n410: | `graphCoverageMode` | `'graph' \\| 'graphless_fallback' \\| 'unavailable_blocked'` | Yes | `graph` uses graph evidence, `graphless_fallback` uses direct text/JSON proof, and `unavailable_blocked` records insufficient fallback proof. |\n411: \n412: ### Search Ledger\n413: \n414: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n415: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n416: | `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n417: | `dimension` | string | Yes | Review dimension addressed by this row. |\n418: | `targetRefs` | string[] | Yes | Targets searched, should overlap `targetSelection.selectedTargets`. |\n419: | `bugClass` | string | Yes | Candidate bug class or invariant family. |\n420: | `hypothesis` / `invariant` | string | Conditional | At least one must be present and non-empty. |\n421: | `searchActions` | array | Yes | Each action has `method`, `queryOrPath`, `result`, and `evidenceRefs`. |\n422: | `disposition` | string | Yes | One of `finding`, `ruled_out`, `deferred`, `blocked`, `not_applicable`. |\n423: | `rationale` | string | Yes | Why this disposition follows from the evidence. |\n424: \n425: | Disposition | Required link | Rule |\n426: |-------------|---------------|------|\n427: | `finding` | `linkedFindingId` | Must reference an `id` present in `findingDetails[]`. |\n428: | `ruled_out` | `ruledOutReason` | Must explain the negative evidence. |\n429: | `deferred` | `deferredReason` | Must explain why later search is acceptable. |\n430: | `blocked` | `blockedReason` | Must name the blocker and expected recovery path. |\n431: | `not_applicable` | `notApplicableReason` | Must explain why the bug class does not apply to this target. |\n432: \n433: Representative v2 record:\n434: \n435: ```json\n436: {\n437:   \"type\": \"iteration\",\n438:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n439:   \"iteration\": 3,\n440:   \"run\": 3,\n441:   \"status\": \"complete\",\n442:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n443:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"],\n444:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n445:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n446:   \"findingDetails\": [],\n447:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0,\n448:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-example\",\n449:   \"generation\": 1,\n450:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n451:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-22T00:00:00Z\",\n452:   \"durationMs\": 120000,\n453:   \"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\": 2,\n454:   \"reviewDepthApplicability\": { \"scopeClass\": \"standard\", \"enforcement\": \"strict\", \"reason\": \"non-trivial state transition target\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n455:   \"targetSelection\": { \"selectedTargets\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"selectionReason\": \"state mutation path under review\", \"discoveryMethods\": [\"direct_read\", \"exact_search\"], \"omittedHighRiskTargets\": [], \"graphStatus\": \"unavailable\", \"semanticSearchStatus\": \"partial\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n456:   \"searchCoverage\": { \"requiredBugClasses\": [\"state_transition\"], \"covered\": [], \"ruledOut\": [\"state_transition\"], \"deferred\": [], \"blocked\": [], \"graphCoverageMode\": \"graphless_fallback\" },\n457:   \"searchLedger\": [{ \"id\": \"SL-001\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"targetRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"bugClass\": \"state_transition\", \"hypothesis\": \"state transition can skip validation\", \"searchActions\": [{ \"method\": \"direct_read\", \"queryOrPath\": \"src/review-target.ts\", \"result\": \"validation guard present on all branches\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:42\"] }], \"disposition\": \"ruled_out\", \"rationale\": \"all mutation branches call the validator\", \"ruledOutReason\": \"guard verified by direct read\" }]\n458: }\n459: ```\n460: \n461: ### Compatibility and Downstream Obligations\n462: \n463: | Record Shape | Reader Behavior | Validator Behavior |\n464: |--------------|-----------------|--------------------|\n465: | v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | Phase D may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n466: | v2 trivial+skip | Parse v2 applicability, `searchLedger: []` allowed with cited scope proof. | Validate `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`, skip ledger-depth requirements. |\n467: | v2 standard/complex | Parse v2 fields in addition to v1 required fields. | Enforce v2 shape, ledger linkage, coverage reconciliation, and evidence refs. |\n468: \n469: Phase E reducer/dashboard/report work must preserve and expose `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, `cleanSearchProof`, and `searchCoverage`. Until Phase E ships, these are contract obligations only. `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and `review-report.md` are not expected to persist them.\n470: \n471: ---\n\n(End of file - total 471 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Review State Log Records\ndescription: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n  - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n  - \"review depth schema\"\n  - \"review traceability checks\"\n  - \"review graph events\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.6\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Log Records\n\nThe `deep-review-state.jsonl` log is the append-only source of truth for a review run. This reference documents the config, iteration, event, and lineage record schemas plus the Review Depth Schema (v2) that the reducer consumes.\n\n---\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Review State Log Records\ndescription: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n  - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n  - \"review depth schema\"\n  - \"review traceability checks\"\n  - \"review graph events\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.6\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Log Records\n\nThe `deep-review-state.jsonl` log is the append-only source of truth for a review run. This reference documents the config, iteration, event, and lineage record schemas plus the Review Depth Schema (v2) that the reducer consumes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n- Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n- Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n- Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n\n### Key Sources\n\n| Source | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n| Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n| Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n| Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n\nAppend-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n\nWhile the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n\n### Line 1: Config Record\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n```\n\nThe projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n\n### Iteration Records\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n  \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"findingsCount\": 4,\n  \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n  \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n  \"findingDetails\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \"path/to/file.ts:42\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Observed consumer still reads the old field.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Update the consumer and add verification.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"cross-consumer\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"rg evidence covering producers and consumers\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"producer/helper\", \"consumer/status\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.32,\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T14:30:00Z\", \"durationMs\": 52000\n}\n```\n\n**Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n\n**Legacy field:** `run`, the older name for `iteration`. Readers still accept it and the fan-out stop-policy validator does not; new records write `iteration`. Event records keep their own `run` field.\n\n**Optional fields:** `parentSessionId`, `continuedFromRun`, `findingsRefined`, `findingRefs`, `traceabilityChecks`, `coverage`, `noveltyJustification`, `ruledOut`, `focusTrack`, `scoreEstimate`, `segment`, `convergenceSignals`, `graphEvents`\n\n| Required Field | Type | Description |\n|---------------|------|-------------|\n| mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n| dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n| filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n| sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n| generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n| lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n| findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n| findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n| findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n| newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n\n### Convergence Signals\n\n| Signal | Weight | Description |\n|--------|--------|-------------|\n| rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n| madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n| dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n| compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n\n**Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n\n### Graph Events\n\nThe optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The MCP coverage graph handlers (`mcp-server/handlers/coverage-graph/upsert.ts`) consume these events and persist them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n  \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n  \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n  \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n  \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"graphEvents\": [\n    { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n    { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n    { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n    { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n    { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n    { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n    { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n  ],\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n  \"durationMs\": 51000\n}\n```\n\n#### Event payload shape\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\n| type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n| id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n| label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n| relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n| source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n| target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n| metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n\n#### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n\n`graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n\nConcrete obligations for producers:\n\n1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n\nThe collision regression in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/session-isolation.vitest.ts` (\"shared-ID collisions\" block) exercises this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows must survive independently.\n\n### Synthesis Event\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n  \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n**Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n\n### Blocked-Stop Event\n\nWhen the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 4,\n  \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n  \"gateResults\": {\n    \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n    \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n      \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n    },\n    \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n    \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n    \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n    \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n    \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n    \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n    \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n  },\n  \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Cover the missing review dimensions, then resolve the active P0.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:45:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n`gateResults` carries the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`: `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. The last two are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. See `../convergence/convergence.md` §Section-1 for the authoritative shape.\n\n**Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n\n### Graph Convergence Event\n\nBefore the inline 3-signal review vote is allowed to finalize STOP, the workflow must append a `graph_convergence` event for the current review lineage.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"graph_convergence\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 4,\n  \"decision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n  \"signals\": {\n    \"dimensionCoverage\": 1,\n    \"findingStability\": 0.88,\n    \"p0ResolutionRate\": 1,\n    \"evidenceDensity\": 1.4,\n    \"hotspotSaturation\": 0.75\n  },\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:44:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n**Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `decision`, `signals`, `blockers`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n\n**Decision enum:** `CONTINUE`, `STOP_ALLOWED`, `STOP_BLOCKED`\n\n**Combined-stop rule:** Final STOP is legal only when the inline review convergence decision says STOP and the latest `graph_convergence.decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\"`. If the latest graph decision is `STOP_BLOCKED`, set `stop_blocked=true`, emit `blocked_stop`, and continue recovery instead of stopping. If the latest graph decision is `CONTINUE`, downgrade the inline STOP candidate to CONTINUE.\n\n### Normalized Pause and Recovery Events\n\nPause and recovery events MUST use the frozen shared stop-reason enum at emission time:\n\n`converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`\n\nRaw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` labels are not legal persisted event names in the review JSONL contract. The workflow must rewrite them before appending JSONL rows.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"userPaused\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"stopReason\": \"userPaused\",\n  \"reason\": \"sentinel file detected\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:32:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"stopReason\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n  \"fromIteration\": 5,\n  \"strategy\": \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\",\n  \"targetDimension\": \"traceability\",\n  \"outcome\": \"pending\",\n  \"reason\": \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:40:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n**Emission rule:** If runtime logic first identifies a raw `paused` or `stuck_recovery` condition, the workflow MUST normalize it to `userPaused` or `stuckRecovery` before writing the JSONL line. Reducers and dashboards may assume persisted event names are already normalized.\n\n### Verdict Rules\n\n| Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n|---------|-----------|--------------|\n| FAIL | `activeP0 > 0` OR quality gate failure | `/speckit:plan` |\n| CONDITIONAL | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 > 0` | `/speckit:plan` |\n| PASS | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` | `/create:changelog` |\n\nWhen `activeP2 > 0` on PASS, set `hasAdvisories: true`.\n\n### traceabilityChecks Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"required\": 2, \"executed\": 3, \"pass\": 1, \"partial\": 1,\n      \"fail\": 1, \"blocked\": 0, \"notApplicable\": 0, \"gatingFailures\": 1\n    },\n    \"results\": [{\n      \"protocolId\": \"spec_code\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n      \"applicable\": true, \"counts\": { \"pass\": 0, \"partial\": 0, \"fail\": 1 },\n      \"evidence\": [\"README.md:48\"], \"findingRefs\": [\"F004\"],\n      \"summary\": \"README claimed the old report contract.\"\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\n| summary.required / executed / pass / partial / fail / blocked / notApplicable | number | Yes | Protocol execution counts |\n| summary.gatingFailures | number | Yes | Hard-gate failures blocking STOP |\n| results[].protocolId | string | Yes | Canonical protocol identifier |\n| results[].status | string | Yes | `pass`, `partial`, `fail`, `blocked`, `notApplicable` |\n| results[].gateClass | string | Yes | `hard` or `advisory` |\n| results[].applicable | boolean | Yes | Whether the protocol applied |\n| results[].counts | object | Yes | Protocol-local summary counts |\n| results[].evidence | string[] | No | Supporting file:line refs |\n| results[].findingRefs | string[] | No | Related finding identifiers |\n| results[].summary | string | Yes | Human-readable one-line result |\n\n### Validation Rules\n\n- Each line must be valid JSON with a `type` field\n- `mode` must be `\"review\"` on all iteration and synthesis records\n- `iteration` values must be sequential. `newFindingsRatio` must be 0.0-1.0\n- `findingsSummary` and `findingsNew` must each contain `P0`, `P1`, `P2` keys\n- `findingDetails` must be an array. Each active item must include `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DEPTH SCHEMA (V2)\n\n`reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2` is the discriminator for the v2 search-depth contract. Absent values, `null`, or any value other than `2` mean v1 legacy: readers keep today's behavior, and validator hard enforcement applies only when the discriminator is present.\n\nFrozen v2 contract:\n\nTop-level review iteration fields when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`:\n- `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`, discriminator\n- `reviewDepthApplicability`, `{ scopeClass: 'trivial'|'standard'|'complex', enforcement: 'strict'|'warn'|'skip', reason: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n- `targetSelection`, `{ selectedTargets: string[], selectionReason: string, discoveryMethods: string[], omittedHighRiskTargets: string[], graphStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', semanticSearchStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n- `searchCoverage`, `{ requiredBugClasses: string[], covered: string[], ruledOut: string[], deferred: string[], blocked: string[], graphCoverageMode: 'graph'|'graphless_fallback'|'unavailable_blocked' }`\n- `searchLedger[]`, array of ledger rows\n\nLedger row fields:\n- Required: `id, dimension, targetRefs, bugClass, disposition, rationale`\n- `hypothesis` (string) OR `invariant` (string), at least one\n- `searchActions[]`, `{ method: string, queryOrPath: string, result: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n- Disposition-specific link (exactly one):\n  - `finding` → `linkedFindingId` (must reference an id present in `findingDetails[]`)\n  - `ruled_out` → `ruledOutReason`\n  - `deferred` → `deferredReason`\n  - `blocked` → `blockedReason`\n  - `not_applicable` → `notApplicableReason`\n\nTrivial-scope exemption: when `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass === 'trivial'` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.enforcement === 'skip'`, ledger may be `[]` with cited scope proof in `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`.\n\n### Applicability\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n|-------|------|----------|-----------|\n| `scopeClass` | `'trivial' \\| 'standard' \\| 'complex'` | Yes | Classifies how much depth proof the review target warrants. |\n| `enforcement` | `'strict' \\| 'warn' \\| 'skip'` | Yes | `strict` means v2 validators fail shallow records, `warn` emits advisory rollout feedback, `skip` is valid only for trivial scope with proof. |\n| `reason` | string | Yes | Human-readable justification for the chosen scope/enforcement pair. |\n| `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | File/path refs proving scope classification, required even for skipped trivial ledgers. |\n\n### Target Selection\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n|-------|------|----------|-----------|\n| `selectedTargets` | string[] | Yes | Files, folders, specs, or surfaces actually searched this iteration. |\n| `selectionReason` | string | Yes | Why these targets were highest-value for the dimension or bug class. |\n| `discoveryMethods` | string[] | Yes | Methods such as direct read, exact search, semantic search, graph query, producer trace, consumer trace, or negative-test search. |\n| `omittedHighRiskTargets` | string[] | Yes | High-risk targets not searched, use `[]` when none were identified. |\n| `graphStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Code/coverage graph availability for this iteration's target selection. |\n| `semanticSearchStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Semantic/code search availability for this iteration. |\n| `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | Evidence for target selection and omitted-target claims. |\n\n### Search Coverage\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n|-------|------|----------|-----------|\n| `requiredBugClasses` | string[] | Yes | Bug classes or invariant families that should be searched for this scope. |\n| `covered` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched with conclusive finding or clean proof. |\n| `ruledOut` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched and explicitly ruled out. |\n| `deferred` | string[] | Yes | Required classes postponed with a reason in ledger rows. |\n| `blocked` | string[] | Yes | Required classes blocked by missing access, graph/search outage, ambiguity, or scope conflict. |\n| `graphCoverageMode` | `'graph' \\| 'graphless_fallback' \\| 'unavailable_blocked'` | Yes | `graph` uses graph evidence, `graphless_fallback` uses direct text/JSON proof, and `unavailable_blocked` records insufficient fallback proof. |\n\n### Search Ledger\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n|-------|------|----------|-----------|\n| `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n| `dimension` | string | Yes | Review dimension addressed by this row. |\n| `targetRefs` | string[] | Yes | Targets searched, should overlap `targetSelection.selectedTargets`. |\n| `bugClass` | string | Yes | Candidate bug class or invariant family. |\n| `hypothesis` / `invariant` | string | Conditional | At least one must be present and non-empty. |\n| `searchActions` | array | Yes | Each action has `method`, `queryOrPath`, `result`, and `evidenceRefs`. |\n| `disposition` | string | Yes | One of `finding`, `ruled_out`, `deferred`, `blocked`, `not_applicable`. |\n| `rationale` | string | Yes | Why this disposition follows from the evidence. |\n\n| Disposition | Required link | Rule |\n|-------------|---------------|------|\n| `finding` | `linkedFindingId` | Must reference an `id` present in `findingDetails[]`. |\n| `ruled_out` | `ruledOutReason` | Must explain the negative evidence. |\n| `deferred` | `deferredReason` | Must explain why later search is acceptable. |\n| `blocked` | `blockedReason` | Must name the blocker and expected recovery path. |\n| `not_applicable` | `notApplicableReason` | Must explain why the bug class does not apply to this target. |\n\nRepresentative v2 record:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"iteration\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"iteration\": 3,\n  \"run\": 3,\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n  \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"],\n  \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n  \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n  \"findingDetails\": [],\n  \"newFindingsRatio\": 0,\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-example\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-22T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"durationMs\": 120000,\n  \"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"reviewDepthApplicability\": { \"scopeClass\": \"standard\", \"enforcement\": \"strict\", \"reason\": \"non-trivial state transition target\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n  \"targetSelection\": { \"selectedTargets\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"selectionReason\": \"state mutation path under review\", \"discoveryMethods\": [\"direct_read\", \"exact_search\"], \"omittedHighRiskTargets\": [], \"graphStatus\": \"unavailable\", \"semanticSearchStatus\": \"partial\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n  \"searchCoverage\": { \"requiredBugClasses\": [\"state_transition\"], \"covered\": [], \"ruledOut\": [\"state_transition\"], \"deferred\": [], \"blocked\": [], \"graphCoverageMode\": \"graphless_fallback\" },\n  \"searchLedger\": [{ \"id\": \"SL-001\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"targetRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"bugClass\": \"state_transition\", \"hypothesis\": \"state transition can skip validation\", \"searchActions\": [{ \"method\": \"direct_read\", \"queryOrPath\": \"src/review-target.ts\", \"result\": \"validation guard present on all branches\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:42\"] }], \"disposition\": \"ruled_out\", \"rationale\": \"all mutation branches call the validator\", \"ruledOutReason\": \"guard verified by direct read\" }]\n}\n```\n\n### Compatibility and Downstream Obligations\n\n| Record Shape | Reader Behavior | Validator Behavior |\n|--------------|-----------------|--------------------|\n| v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | Phase D may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n| v2 trivial+skip | Parse v2 applicability, `searchLedger: []` allowed with cited scope proof. | Validate `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`, skip ledger-depth requirements. |\n| v2 standard/complex | Parse v2 fields in addition to v1 required fields. | Enforce v2 shape, ledger linkage, coverage reconciliation, and evidence refs. |\n\nPhase E reducer/dashboard/report work must preserve and expose `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, `cleanSearchProof`, and `searchCoverage`. Until Phase E ships, these are contract obligations only. `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and `review-report.md` are not expected to persist them.\n\n---","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":471,"totalLines":471,"truncated":false}},"title":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md","time":{"start":1792421569981,"end":1792421569985}},"id":"prt_154a6a50a001gWz1ZMMXLvIMCB","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a68de1001w9pA0IkGp81G17"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421570140,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_dwXca9zr3TuAnm5ROdgY2678","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"topic\": \"\",\n3:   \"sessionId\": \"\",\n4:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n5:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n6:   \"generation\": 1,\n7:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n8:   \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n9:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n10:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n11:   \"antiConvergence\": {\n12:     \"minIterations\": 2,\n13:     \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n14:     \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n15:   },\n16:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n17:   \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n18:   \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n19:   \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n20:   \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n21:   \"specFolder\": \"\",\n22:   \"createdAt\": \"\",\n23:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n24:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n25:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n26:   \"executor\": {\n27:     \"kind\": \"native\",\n28:     \"model\": null,\n29:     \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n30:     \"serviceTier\": null,\n31:     \"sandboxMode\": null,\n32:     \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n33:   },\n34:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n35:   \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n36:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n37:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\n38:     \"correctness\",\n39:     \"security\",\n40:     \"traceability\",\n41:     \"maintainability\"\n42:   ],\n43:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n44:   \"crossReference\": {\n45:     \"core\": [\n46:       \"spec_code\",\n47:       \"checklist_evidence\"\n48:     ],\n49:     \"overlay\": [\n50:       \"skill_agent\",\n51:       \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n52:       \"feature_catalog_code\",\n53:       \"playbook_capability\"\n54:     ]\n55:   },\n56:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n57:   \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n58:   \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n59:   \"fileProtection\": {\n60:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n61:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n62:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n63:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n64:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n65:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n66:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n67:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n68:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n69:   },\n70:   \"reducer\": {\n71:     \"enabled\": true,\n72:     \"inputs\": [\n73:       \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n74:       \"newIterationFile\",\n75:       \"priorReducedState\"\n76:     ],\n77:     \"outputs\": [\n78:       \"findingsRegistry\",\n79:       \"dashboardMetrics\",\n80:       \"strategyUpdates\"\n81:     ],\n82:     \"metrics\": [\n83:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n84:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n85:       \"openFindings\",\n86:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n87:       \"convergenceScore\"\n88:     ]\n89:   },\n90:   \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n91:     \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n92:     \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n93:     \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n94:     \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n95:     \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n96:   }\n97: }\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json","text":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 7,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n  \"crossReference\": {\n    \"core\": [\n      \"spec_code\",\n      \"checklist_evidence\"\n    ],\n    \"overlay\": [\n      \"skill_agent\",\n      \"agent_cross_runtime\",\n      \"feature_catalog_code\",\n      \"playbook_capability\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n    \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"latestJSONLDelta\",\n      \"newIterationFile\",\n      \"priorReducedState\"\n    ],\n    \"outputs\": [\n      \"findingsRegistry\",\n      \"dashboardMetrics\",\n      \"strategyUpdates\"\n    ],\n    \"metrics\": [\n      \"dimensionsCovered\",\n      \"findingsBySeverity\",\n      \"openFindings\",\n      \"resolvedFindings\",\n      \"convergenceScore\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineageMode\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"mode\", \"reviewDimensions\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":97,"totalLines":97,"truncated":false}},"title":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json","time":{"start":1792421570135,"end":1792421570139}},"id":"prt_154a6a5c7001HurVKbv5mVVy0d","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a68de1001w9pA0IkGp81G17"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421570315,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_AP80zcP7TjQdR4uKqyoA6827","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```\n\n(End of file - total 218 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review strategy template\"\n  - \"review dimension tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n  - \"review session tracking\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.11.0.13\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review strategy template\"\n  - \"review dimension tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n  - \"review session tracking\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.11.0.13\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n- **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n- **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n[Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n[What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n- What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n\n### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n- What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n- Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n- [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n[Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\nPopulate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n\n- Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n- Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n- Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n- Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n\nDo not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: [from config]\n- Convergence threshold: [from config]\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n- Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n- Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n- Started: [timestamp]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n\nReference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n\n```markdown\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n- Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n- Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n- Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n- Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n\n## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: test-coverage\n- Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n- Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n\n## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n| Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n|----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n| correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n| test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n| cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n| observability        | converging | 4                  |\n```","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":218,"totalLines":218,"truncated":false}},"title":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md","time":{"start":1792421570308,"end":1792421570313}},"id":"prt_154a6a673001U1t6GwvrK8gLrd","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a68de1001w9pA0IkGp81G17"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1792421571604,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"id":"prt_154a6ac12001LUU5IfFA1V7y95","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"175d1b1e5163eab067d20ca1e4c25960e6435fa4","messageID":"msg_154a68de1001w9pA0IkGp81G17","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":110565,"input":23938,"output":441,"reasoning":426,"cache":{"write":0,"read":85760}},"cost":0.003931362}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792421576002,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"id":"prt_154a6bd4000186ZxkWMzSj5fIg","messageID":"msg_154a6b091001Ty46xPOAdNaQ5P","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","snapshot":"175d1b1e5163eab067d20ca1e4c25960e6435fa4","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421577205,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_JlOY7jlQmRphMRgJCO4A7104","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"phase_init\\|step_init\\|synthesis\\|stopReason\\|run_initialized\\|fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\\|append-mode-event\\|type.*config\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml | head -120","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review"},"output":"8:action: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\n39:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n45:  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n99:  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n159:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n162:        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n163:        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n165:        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n176:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n202:    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n212:      deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n215:      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n217:      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n237:  phase_init:\n297:        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir} && if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}; find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; ; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}; [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}; if [ -e {state_paths.state_log} ]; then MIGRATION_EVENT=$(mktemp); GATEWAY=.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs; [ -f \\\"$GATEWAY\\\" ] || GATEWAY=scripts/append-mode-event.cjs; printf '%s\\n' '{\\\"stem\\\":\\\"deep_review.migration\\\",\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"runId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"{session_id}\\\"},\\\"data\\\":{\\\"mode\\\":\\\"review\\\",\\\"legacyArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-research-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-research-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-research-pause\\\"],\\\"canonicalArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-review-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-review-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-review-pause\\\"]}}' > \\\"$MIGRATION_EVENT\\\"; node \\\"$GATEWAY\\\" --mode review --run-directory \\\"$(dirname {state_paths.state_log})\\\" --event-json \\\"$MIGRATION_EVENT\\\"; MIGRATION_STATUS=$?; rm -f \\\"$MIGRATION_EVENT\\\"; [ \\\"$MIGRATION_STATUS\\\" -eq 0 ] || exit \\\"$MIGRATION_STATUS\\\"; fi; fi; find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; 2>/dev/null || true\"\n349:          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n350:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n468:        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n477:          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n478:          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n489:              stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n515:        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n547:        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n567:      step_init_complete:\n639:          bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n683:               stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n688:             a) if iteration_count >= max_iterations: set decision = \"STOP\", stopReason = \"maxIterationsReached\", hard_stop_reason = \"max_iterations_reached\", preserve any failed legal-stop gates as terminal evidence, and proceed to synthesis without legal-stop veto\n691:             Operator stop reasons (`maxIterationsReached`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, unrecoverable `error`) are terminal ceilings. They do not hide failed gates; they record them in synthesis and stop dispatch.\n726:               stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n758:                    stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n999:                action: \"Adopt a successful read-only review direction or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n1010:                  log: \"Divergent review pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n1011:                  skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1013:              log: \"Divergent review pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n1014:              skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1017:            skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1328:            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1329:            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1634:            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, and write the iteration file, the delta and the state record exactly as the leaf contract requires, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1992:            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1993:            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1996:            {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\