 \"session-end-arm.mjs\"\n.hermes/SYNC.md:79:| `pre_llm_call` | `bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, `spec-gate/devin/spec-gate-classify.mjs`, `session-relaunch/hermes/context-nudge.mjs` | Prepends the session-relaunch claim-seed instructions on a `[session-relaunch]` first turn or the handoff nudge once the fill crosses the threshold, then appends the skill-advisor brief and classifies the prompt for the Gate 3 spec-folder gate. The classification is skipped for an orchestrated leaf, whose write authority is already bound to a lineage directory. The question itself never rides this channel. It reaches the model once at the first mutation |\n.hermes/SYNC.md:80:| `post_api_request` | per-session usage record held by the plugin | Keeps the latest completed call's `usage` and model under the session id. It stores the reported context window when present and resolves a missing window from Hermes model metadata using the model, provider and base URL. The next `pre_llm_call` uses the record to compute the session-relaunch fill ratio. No model-visible output |\n.hermes/SYNC.md:86:| `on_session_end` | `dist/hooks/devin/session-stop.js`, `session-cleanup/devin/session-cleanup.sh`, `session-relaunch/hermes/session-end-arm.mjs` | The adapter accepts a missing event name from the bridge and rejects a supplied name other than `on_session_end`. It arms a pending session-relaunch record for this session under `SKILLED_LOOP_ID` before detaching the killer, so a spawn failure leaves the record armed. Hermes fires this event after every message. The hook also records the closing state and reaps the MCP helpers this Hermes process spawned |\n","metadata":{"output":"        \"extension\": null,\n        \"reason\": \"Cursor's sessionEnd persistence; Pi persists on session_shutdown in session-stop-context.ts\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"session-relaunch\",\n      \"concern\": \"Hand a session near its context limit to a fresh one under skilled-loop\",\n      \"bindings\": {\n        \