{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421756661,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_br8SJOyvQXOTmQQ25iL91828","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -ld .skilled/skills/.state .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs 2>/dev/null; ls -l .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs 2>/dev/null | head; grep -n \"state\" .gitignore | head -10; echo \"=== repo claude\"; ls CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"runtime state\" AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review"},"output":"drwxr-xr-x@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff  288 Oct 19 16:46 .skilled/skills/.state\n124:# Runtime state folders (plugin / tooling state)\n128:# Excluding the .state directories themselves would make the README negation\n131:.opencode/skills/.state/*/*\n132:.skilled/skills/.state/*/*\n133:!.opencode/skills/.state/*/README.md\n134:!.skilled/skills/.state/*/README.md\n135:# Pre-consolidation state directories still written by some tooling. They are\n137:.opencode/skills/.authority-state/\n138:.skilled/skills/.authority-state/\n139:.opencode/skills/.spec-gate-state/\n=== repo claude\nAGENTS.md:70:- **Artifact trigger — binds on what you are about to write, independently of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs, which are `system-spec-kit`'s, and gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what the router resolves, under the same loading rule as Gate 5. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract that is wrong for this case is followed and amended, as PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4 says.\nAGENTS.md:75:**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n","metadata":{"output":"drwxr-xr-x@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff  288 Oct 19 16:46 .skilled/skills/.state\n124:# Runtime state folders (plugin / tooling state)\n128:# Excluding the .state directories themselves would make the README negation\n131:.opencode/skills/.state/*/*\n132:.skilled/skills/.state/*/*\n133:!.opencode/skills/.state/*/README.md\n134:!.skilled/skills/.state/*/README.md\n135:# Pre-consolidation state directories still written by some tooling. They are\n137:.opencode/skills/.authority-state/\n138:.skilled/skills/.authority-state/\n139:.opencode/skills/.spec-gate-state/\n=== repo claude\nAGENTS.md:70:- **Artifact trigger — binds on what you are about to write, independently of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs, which are `system-spec-kit`'s, and gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what the router resolves, under the same loading rule as Gate 5. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract that is wrong for this case is followed and amended, as PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4 says.\nAGENTS.md:75:**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -ld .skilled/skills/.state .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs 2>/dev/null; ls -l .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs 2>/dev/null | head; grep -n \"state\" .gitignore | head -10; echo \"=== repo claude\"; ls CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"runtime state\" AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head","time":{"start":1792421756629,"end":1792421756660}},"id":"prt_154a97cfa001aCmvNzyge6Pkis","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a962da0013HmJznPrlfw2YO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421757238,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_ccTIRwIV0bCa7BoY2qxV0791","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"save.*handoff\\|handoff.*save\\|/speckit:save\" AGENTS.md .claude/CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head; echo \"=== hooks flags file\"; ls -l .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env 2>/dev/null; echo; grep -rn \"SESSION_RELAUNCH\" .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md 2>/dev/null | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review"},"output":"AGENTS.md:75:**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\nAGENTS.md:148:Trigger: \"save context\", \"save memory\", `/speckit:save`\nAGENTS.md:151:- The save runs the continuity writer `generate-context.js` through `/speckit:save`. Composition, what the writer touches and the post-save review are `system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md`'s. HIGH review issues are patched by hand.\n=== hooks flags file\n\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:98:| `SYSTEM_SESSION_RELAUNCH_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the session-relaunch hooks: context nudge and stop arm. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:108:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD` | `0.80` | number (0..1) | Fraction of the effective context window that triggers the handoff nudge. Keep it well above a fresh session's startup fill plus its remaining work. Codex live runs chained at `0.12` because each fresh session reached about 10% on startup alone. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:109:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS` | (unset) | number (positive int, tokens) | Overrides the effective context window the fill ratio is measured against. Unset resolves `autoCompactWindow` from the Claude settings files, then the model default. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:110:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS` | `10` | number (non-negative int) | Relaunches allowed per `skilled-loop` run. The cap is enforced at three points: the wrapper declines a record at or above it, `prepare` writes no record and exits 3 with the manual claim command, and the killer unarms the record with reason `hop-cap` and sends no signal. Adapters stop nudging at the cap. Zero is accepted and declines every hop. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:111:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_AGE_MIN` | `10` | number (minutes) | Minutes an armed relaunch file stays valid. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:112:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_REPO_ROOT` | (unset) | string (absolute path) | Repository root that planned handoff note paths resolve under. Unset falls back to the install root that holds the concern, so a runtime started in a subdirectory still writes under the repo root. The generic `REPO_ROOT` is not read. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n","metadata":{"output":"AGENTS.md:75:**Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`, such as a session-relaunch handoff note. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\nAGENTS.md:148:Trigger: \"save context\", \"save memory\", `/speckit:save`\nAGENTS.md:151:- The save runs the continuity writer `generate-context.js` through `/speckit:save`. Composition, what the writer touches and the post-save review are `system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md`'s. HIGH review issues are patched by hand.\n=== hooks flags file\n\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:98:| `SYSTEM_SESSION_RELAUNCH_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the session-relaunch hooks: context nudge and stop arm. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:108:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD` | `0.80` | number (0..1) | Fraction of the effective context window that triggers the handoff nudge. Keep it well above a fresh session's startup fill plus its remaining work. Codex live runs chained at `0.12` because each fresh session reached about 10% on startup alone. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:109:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS` | (unset) | number (positive int, tokens) | Overrides the effective context window the fill ratio is measured against. Unset resolves `autoCompactWindow` from the Claude settings files, then the model default. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:110:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS` | `10` | number (non-negative int) | Relaunches allowed per `skilled-loop` run. The cap is enforced at three points: the wrapper declines a record at or above it, `prepare` writes no record and exits 3 with the manual claim command, and the killer unarms the record with reason `hop-cap` and sends no signal. Adapters stop nudging at the cap. Zero is accepted and declines every hop. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:111:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_AGE_MIN` | `10` | number (minutes) | Minutes an armed relaunch file stays valid. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:112:| `SESSION_RELAUNCH_REPO_ROOT` | (unset) | string (absolute path) | Repository root that planned handoff note paths resolve under. Unset falls back to the install root that holds the concern, so a runtime started in a subdirectory still writes under the repo root. The generic `REPO_ROOT` is not read. | `.skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/` |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"save.*handoff\\|handoff.*save\\|/speckit:save\" AGENTS.md .claude/CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head; echo \"=== hooks flags file\"; ls -l .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env 2>/dev/null; echo; grep -rn \"SESSION_RELAUNCH\" .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md 2>/dev/null | head -30","time":{"start":1792421757207,"end":1792421757237}},"id":"prt_154a97ede001l3SPhpgnWAruic","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154a962da0013HmJznPrlfw2YO"}}
