w session. Tell me when you are ready. The task: read .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md and .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/killer.cjs in full, summarize each in three bullets, then report the README line count and its first heading. Gate 3: D) Skip, no spec folder.'; echo WRAPPER_EXIT=\\$?; exec bash\"; sleep 8; tmux capture-pane -p -t sr-codex | grep -q \"Hooks need review\" && tmux send-keys -t sr-codex Down Enter && echo codex-hooks-trusted; echo started\n\n## 2026-10-19T08:14:58.164Z\nSP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/5820adf5-6b90-452d-9421-385ec95d7f40/scratchpad; W=/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/142-session-relaunch-loop; PR='Carry this short task through a context handoff, then finish it in the new session. Do not do the task in this session: when the handoff nudge arrives, write the note and prepare the relaunch. The task: report the line count of .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md and name its first heading. Gate 3: D) Skip, no spec folder.'; bash $SP/pb3/clean-tmux.sh sr-pi \"cd '$W' && PATH='$W/.skilled/bin':\\$PATH SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD=0.05 SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS=100 SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS=1 skilled-loop pi --provider openai --model gpt-6-luna '$PR'; echo WRAPPER_EXIT=\\$?; exec bash\"; echo started\n\n## 2026-10-19T08:51:53.396Z\nSP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/5820adf5-6b90-452d-9421-385ec95d7f40/scratchpad; W=/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/142-session-relaunch-loop; cd $W; md5 -q .opencode/package.json; ls .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs/ | wc -l; bash $SP/pb3/clean-tmux.sh sr-pi5 \"cd $W && SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD=0.05 SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS=100 SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS=1 PATH=$W/.skilled/bin:\\$PATH skilled-loop pi --provider openai --model gpt-6-luna 'Read .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/README.md and summarize its first section in two sentences. This is a read-only task; no spec folder is needed.'; echo WRAPPER_EXIT=\\$?; sleep 600\"; echo started\n\n=== playbook claude command\n44:| session-relaunch-claude | Claude session relaunch | Live: follow a prepared note through a tmux relaunch. | Start a short task. Follow the session-relaunch nudge. Finish the remaining work in the receiving Claude session. | tmux new-session -d -s session-relaunch-check 'SESSION_RELAUNCH_THRESHOLD=0.05 SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS=100 SESSION_RELAUNCH_MAX_HOPS=1 bash .skilled/bin/skilled-loop claude \"Carry this short task through the handoff and finish it in the receiving session.\"'<br>tmux attach -t session-relaunch-check | Prepare exits 0 and writes pending. Stop arms the record after the transcript path is present and background tasks have drained. The wrapper starts Claude with the claim seed. The note reaches done. | Capture the tmux pane and handoff status changes. Save relevant relaunch.log entries. | PASS when the same handoff reaches done after a new Claude process starts with the seed. FAIL when an eligible armed record is declined or the note cannot be claimed. | Check note frontmatter and sections. Check Stop session id, runtime log and hop or age decline reason. |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/evidence/live-run10-2026-10-19/launch-commands.txt 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== 006 launch commands\"; cat specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/006-deep-review-2-remediation/evidence/live-runs-2026-10-19/launch-commands.txt 2>/dev/null | head -30; echo \"=== playbook claude command\"; grep -n \"tmux_command\\|skilled-loop claude\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/plugins-and-hooks/session-relaunch-claude.md | head -10","time":{"start":1792421906536,"end":1792421906633}},"id":"prt_154abc5f0001f9XN4hQIjZIg0u","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","