{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792421933132,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"id":"prt_154ac304a001kF7ZufOt4Ys861","messageID":"msg_154ac247f001yufM05azF2EZC9","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","snapshot":"017658fdbb52f28ffd0360a66f33e3ed9d40b1a3","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792421935641,"sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_am7oAaeS9bels1Ykyg9v0640","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat -n .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md | sed -n '1,220p'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/148-session-relaunch-deep-review"},"output":"     1\t---\n     2\tdescription: \"Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop: the manual trigger on every runtime.\"\n     3\targument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n     4\tallowed-tools: Read, Write, Bash\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# /speckit:handoff\n     8\t\n     9\tManual entry point for the session relaunch loop. Writes this session's handoff note and prepares a pending record. Automatic runtimes arm it at their end event. Command-only runtimes leave it pending and use a manual claim command.\n    10\t\n    11\t---\n    12\t\n    13\t## 1. PURPOSE\n    14\t\n    15\tThe relaunch loop carries work into a fresh session near the end of this session's useful context. This session writes a standalone handoff note. The wrapper relaunches the runtime with a claim seed. The new session picks up the remaining work. This command is the manual trigger on runtimes wired with the session-relaunch hooks and the only trigger on runtimes without a hook. Section 5 covers a session seeded with `[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>`.\n    16\t\n    17\t---\n    18\t\n    19\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    20\t\n    21\t**Inputs:** nothing through `$ARGUMENTS`. Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. On Claude, `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check. Other runtimes must pass the session id. If a runtime has no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that id for the session. `spec_folder` records the Gate 3 answer: the repo-relative packet path, `none` after D) Skip or empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n    22\t\n    23\t**Outputs:**\n    24\t\n    25\t- A handoff note at `.skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs/<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>-<first 8 chars of the session id>.md`.\n    26\t- One `STATUS=` line per the exit code in Step 5.\n    27\t- When a spec packet is bound: save continuity before the note is written. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to the continuity writer.\n    28\t\n    29\t**CLI:** `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs`\n    30\t\n    31\t| Invocation | Effect | Exit |\n    32\t|---|---|---|\n    33\t| `prepare --handoff <path> --session <id> [--runtime <name>]` | Validate the note and write the pending relaunch record | `0` prepared (pending until an automatic arm event, or manual on command-only runtimes), `2` refused (reason on stderr, including a runtime conflict), `3` not under `skilled-loop` |\n    34\t| `claim <path> --session <id>` | Move the note `open -> claimed` and print its body | `0` ok, `2` refused |\n    35\t| `complete <path>` | Move the note `claimed -> done` | `0` ok, `2` refused |\n    36\t\n    37\t---\n    38\t\n    39\t## 3. WORKFLOW OVERVIEW\n    40\t\n    41\t| Step | Name | Purpose | Output |\n    42\t|---|---|---|---|\n    43\t| 1 | Resolve inputs | Session id, cwd, spec binding | Values for the note |\n    44\t| 2 | Save the packet | Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes use the continuity writer when a packet is bound | Fresh continuity |\n    45\t| 3 | Write the note | `status: open` handoff file | The note path |\n    46\t| 4 | Prepare | CLI validates and records | Exit code `0`, `2` or `3` |\n    47\t| 5 | Report | Translate the exit code | `STATUS=` line |\n    48\t\n    49\t---\n    50\t\n    51\t## 4. INSTRUCTIONS\n    52\t\n    53\t### Step 1: Resolve inputs\n    54\t\n    55\t- Session id: both commands require `--session <id>`. Claude Code can omit the flag because the CLI reads `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. If a runtime exposes no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that value for the rest of the session. The id fills the note's `session_id`, the filename suffix and `--session`.\n    56\t- cwd: the absolute working directory.\n    57\t- Spec binding: use the repo-relative packet path when one is bound. Use `none` when Gate 3 was answered D) Skip. Leave the field empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n    58\t\n    59\t### Step 2: Save the bound packet\n    60\t\n    61\tWhen `spec_folder` is a packet path, save its continuity before writing the note so the receiving session's `/speckit:resume` lands on fresh state. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`. Record the repo-relative packet path in `spec_folder`. When Gate 3 was answered D) Skip, set `spec_folder` to `none` and skip the save. When Gate 3 was never answered, leave `spec_folder` empty.\n    62\t\n    63\t### Step 3: Write the handoff note\n    64\t\n    65\tCreate the directory first:\n    66\t\n    67\t```bash\n    68\tmkdir -p .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\tName the file `<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>-<first 8 chars of session id>.md`. `date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ` produces the stamp and `${SESSION_ID:0:8}` the suffix. The note format is exact:\n    72\t\n    73\t```markdown\n    74\t---\n    75\tstatus: open\n    76\tsession_id: <id of the session that wrote it>\n    77\tloop_id: <SKILLED_LOOP_ID or empty>\n    78\truntime: <runtime-name>\n    79\tcwd: <absolute cwd>\n    80\tspec_folder: <repo-relative packet path, none if Gate 3 was answered D) Skip or empty if Gate 3 was never answered>\n    81\tcreated_at: <ISO-8601 UTC>\n    82\t---\n    83\t## Goal\n    84\t<non-empty>\n    85\t## Done\n    86\t<non-empty>\n    87\t## Remaining work\n    88\t<non-empty>\n    89\t## In-flight state\n    90\t<non-empty>\n    91\t```\n    92\t\n    93\tFrontmatter is flat `key: value` lines only: no nesting, no lists. `loop_id` is `$SKILLED_LOOP_ID`, empty when the session is not running under the wrapper. `runtime` is the runtime that wrote the note. Every section must be non-empty. Goal states what the work is for. Done records finished work. Remaining work lists the claimable tail. In-flight state preserves the active work the next session must not lose, including open files, half-applied edits, running processes and pending decisions.\n    94\t\n    95\t### Step 4: Prepare\n    96\t\n    97\t```bash\n    98\tnode .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs prepare --handoff <path> --session <session id> --runtime <runtime>\n    99\t```\n   100\t\n   101\tPass `--session <id>` to `prepare`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The `--runtime` value must be one of `claude`, `pi`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `hermes` or `devin`. Outside the loop, it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, it must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The handoff nudge passes the session id and runtime.\n   102\t\n   103\t### Step 5: Report by exit code\n   104\t\n   105\t- `0`: prepared. The record is pending until the runtime's arm event fires. Command-only runtimes leave it pending for the wrapper's manual command. Report `STATUS=OK RESULT=prepared HANDOFF=<path>` and stop.\n   106\t- `2`: refused. Show the stderr reason verbatim. Fix the cause it names, then run `prepare` again. The cause may be an invalid note, a note owned by another session or a live shell child of the runtime process. Report `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"<reason>\"` only when the refusal cannot be repaired.\n   107\t- `3`: not running under `skilled-loop`. The CLI prints the command for the selected runtime. Show it verbatim and report `STATUS=OK RESULT=manual HANDOFF=<path>`.\n   108\t\n   109\t| Runtime | Printed command |\n   110\t|---|---|\n   111\t| Claude | `skilled-loop claude \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   112\t| Pi | `skilled-loop pi \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   113\t| OpenCode | `skilled-loop opencode --prompt \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   114\t| Codex | `skilled-loop codex \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   115\t| Cursor | `skilled-loop cursor \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   116\t| Hermes | `skilled-loop hermes chat -q \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   117\t| Devin | `skilled-loop devin -- \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   118\t\n   119\tThe CLI and wrapper place each path `!` in single quotes outside the seed's double quotes. For example, they print `skilled-loop claude \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff /tmp/han\"'!'\"doff.md\"`. Interactive Bash keeps that path intact when history expansion is on.\n   120\t\n   121\t---\n   122\t\n   123\t## 5. RECEIVING A HANDOFF\n   124\t\n   125\tA session seeded with `[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>` is on the other side of this protocol. It:\n   126\t\n   127\t1. Runs `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs claim <path> --session <session id>`, which moves the note `open -> claimed` and prints its body. Only Claude Code may omit `--session` and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. A runtime without a session-id variable generates an id with `uuidgen` and reuses it for the session.\n   128\t2. Reads the note's Goal, Done, Remaining work and In-flight state sections.\n   129\t3. Runs `/speckit:resume <spec_folder>` when the field contains a repo-relative packet path. When it is `none`, Gate 3 was answered D) Skip and the receiver does not ask it again. When it is empty, Gate 3 was never answered and the receiver asks it as usual.\n   130\t4. Continues the Remaining work.\n   131\t5. Runs `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs complete <path>` when the handoff is fully absorbed.\n   132\t\n   133\tThe note's status moves only `open -> claimed -> done`. When this session prepares a successor hop, `prepare` marks every other note this session claimed as `done`, sets `completed_at` and adds `superseded_by` with the new note's basename. It leaves open notes, done notes, notes claimed by another session and the new note unchanged.\n   134\t\n   135\t---\n   136\t\n   137\t## 6. EXAMPLES\n   138\t\n   139\t**Example 1: inside the loop**\n   140\t\n   141\t```text\n   142\t/speckit:handoff\n   143\t```\n   144\t\n   145\tThe note is written and `prepare` exits `0`. On an automatic runtime, its arm event can qualify the record for relaunch when the session ends.\n   146\t\n   147\t**Example 2: outside the loop**\n   148\t\n   149\t```text\n   150\t/speckit:handoff\n   151\t```\n   152\t\n   153\t`prepare` exits `3` and the command shows the selected runtime's printed claim command so the operator can run the hop by hand.\n   154\t\n   155\t---\n   156\t\n   157\t## 7. RELATED COMMANDS\n   158\t\n   159\t- `/speckit:save`: used before the note on Claude when a spec packet is bound. Other runtimes use the continuity writer.\n   160\t- `/speckit:resume`: runs on the receiving side when the note names a `spec_folder`.\n","metadata":{"output":"     1\t---\n     2\tdescription: \"Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop: the manual trigger on every runtime.\"\n     3\targument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n     4\tallowed-tools: Read, Write, Bash\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# /speckit:handoff\n     8\t\n     9\tManual entry point for the session relaunch loop. Writes this session's handoff note and prepares a pending record. Automatic runtimes arm it at their end event. Command-only runtimes leave it pending and use a manual claim command.\n    10\t\n    11\t---\n    12\t\n    13\t## 1. PURPOSE\n    14\t\n    15\tThe relaunch loop carries work into a fresh session near the end of this session's useful context. This session writes a standalone handoff note. The wrapper relaunches the runtime with a claim seed. The new session picks up the remaining work. This command is the manual trigger on runtimes wired with the session-relaunch hooks and the only trigger on runtimes without a hook. Section 5 covers a session seeded with `[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>`.\n    16\t\n    17\t---\n    18\t\n    19\t## 2. CONTRACT\n    20\t\n    21\t**Inputs:** nothing through `$ARGUMENTS`. Both `prepare` and `claim` require `--session <id>`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. On Claude, `CLAUDE_PID` supplies the runtime process id for the shell-child check. Other runtimes must pass the session id. If a runtime has no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that id for the session. `spec_folder` records the Gate 3 answer: the repo-relative packet path, `none` after D) Skip or empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n    22\t\n    23\t**Outputs:**\n    24\t\n    25\t- A handoff note at `.skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs/<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>-<first 8 chars of the session id>.md`.\n    26\t- One `STATUS=` line per the exit code in Step 5.\n    27\t- When a spec packet is bound: save continuity before the note is written. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to the continuity writer.\n    28\t\n    29\t**CLI:** `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs`\n    30\t\n    31\t| Invocation | Effect | Exit |\n    32\t|---|---|---|\n    33\t| `prepare --handoff <path> --session <id> [--runtime <name>]` | Validate the note and write the pending relaunch record | `0` prepared (pending until an automatic arm event, or manual on command-only runtimes), `2` refused (reason on stderr, including a runtime conflict), `3` not under `skilled-loop` |\n    34\t| `claim <path> --session <id>` | Move the note `open -> claimed` and print its body | `0` ok, `2` refused |\n    35\t| `complete <path>` | Move the note `claimed -> done` | `0` ok, `2` refused |\n    36\t\n    37\t---\n    38\t\n    39\t## 3. WORKFLOW OVERVIEW\n    40\t\n    41\t| Step | Name | Purpose | Output |\n    42\t|---|---|---|---|\n    43\t| 1 | Resolve inputs | Session id, cwd, spec binding | Values for the note |\n    44\t| 2 | Save the packet | Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes use the continuity writer when a packet is bound | Fresh continuity |\n    45\t| 3 | Write the note | `status: open` handoff file | The note path |\n    46\t| 4 | Prepare | CLI validates and records | Exit code `0`, `2` or `3` |\n    47\t| 5 | Report | Translate the exit code | `STATUS=` line |\n    48\t\n    49\t---\n    50\t\n    51\t## 4. INSTRUCTIONS\n    52\t\n    53\t### Step 1: Resolve inputs\n    54\t\n    55\t- Session id: both commands require `--session <id>`. Claude Code can omit the flag because the CLI reads `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. Other runtimes pass the id directly. If a runtime exposes no session-id variable, such as Devin or Cursor, run `uuidgen` once and reuse that value for the rest of the session. The id fills the note's `session_id`, the filename suffix and `--session`.\n    56\t- cwd: the absolute working directory.\n    57\t- Spec binding: use the repo-relative packet path when one is bound. Use `none` when Gate 3 was answered D) Skip. Leave the field empty when Gate 3 was never answered.\n    58\t\n    59\t### Step 2: Save the bound packet\n    60\t\n    61\tWhen `spec_folder` is a packet path, save its continuity before writing the note so the receiving session's `/speckit:resume` lands on fresh state. Claude runs `/speckit:save`. Other runtimes pipe the save JSON to `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin --full-auto <spec-folder>`. Record the repo-relative packet path in `spec_folder`. When Gate 3 was answered D) Skip, set `spec_folder` to `none` and skip the save. When Gate 3 was never answered, leave `spec_folder` empty.\n    62\t\n    63\t### Step 3: Write the handoff note\n    64\t\n    65\tCreate the directory first:\n    66\t\n    67\t```bash\n    68\tmkdir -p .skilled/skills/.state/session-relaunch/handoffs\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\tName the file `<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>-<first 8 chars of session id>.md`. `date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ` produces the stamp and `${SESSION_ID:0:8}` the suffix. The note format is exact:\n    72\t\n    73\t```markdown\n    74\t---\n    75\tstatus: open\n    76\tsession_id: <id of the session that wrote it>\n    77\tloop_id: <SKILLED_LOOP_ID or empty>\n    78\truntime: <runtime-name>\n    79\tcwd: <absolute cwd>\n    80\tspec_folder: <repo-relative packet path, none if Gate 3 was answered D) Skip or empty if Gate 3 was never answered>\n    81\tcreated_at: <ISO-8601 UTC>\n    82\t---\n    83\t## Goal\n    84\t<non-empty>\n    85\t## Done\n    86\t<non-empty>\n    87\t## Remaining work\n    88\t<non-empty>\n    89\t## In-flight state\n    90\t<non-empty>\n    91\t```\n    92\t\n    93\tFrontmatter is flat `key: value` lines only: no nesting, no lists. `loop_id` is `$SKILLED_LOOP_ID`, empty when the session is not running under the wrapper. `runtime` is the runtime that wrote the note. Every section must be non-empty. Goal states what the work is for. Done records finished work. Remaining work lists the claimable tail. In-flight state preserves the active work the next session must not lose, including open files, half-applied edits, running processes and pending decisions.\n    94\t\n    95\t### Step 4: Prepare\n    96\t\n    97\t```bash\n    98\tnode .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs prepare --handoff <path> --session <session id> --runtime <runtime>\n    99\t```\n   100\t\n   101\tPass `--session <id>` to `prepare`. Only Claude Code can omit it and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The `--runtime` value must be one of `claude`, `pi`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `hermes` or `devin`. Outside the loop, it overrides the environment or Claude default. Inside the loop, it must match `SKILLED_LOOP_RUNTIME` or prepare exits 2. The handoff nudge passes the session id and runtime.\n   102\t\n   103\t### Step 5: Report by exit code\n   104\t\n   105\t- `0`: prepared. The record is pending until the runtime's arm event fires. Command-only runtimes leave it pending for the wrapper's manual command. Report `STATUS=OK RESULT=prepared HANDOFF=<path>` and stop.\n   106\t- `2`: refused. Show the stderr reason verbatim. Fix the cause it names, then run `prepare` again. The cause may be an invalid note, a note owned by another session or a live shell child of the runtime process. Report `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"<reason>\"` only when the refusal cannot be repaired.\n   107\t- `3`: not running under `skilled-loop`. The CLI prints the command for the selected runtime. Show it verbatim and report `STATUS=OK RESULT=manual HANDOFF=<path>`.\n   108\t\n   109\t| Runtime | Printed command |\n   110\t|---|---|\n   111\t| Claude | `skilled-loop claude \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   112\t| Pi | `skilled-loop pi \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   113\t| OpenCode | `skilled-loop opencode --prompt \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   114\t| Codex | `skilled-loop codex \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   115\t| Cursor | `skilled-loop cursor \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   116\t| Hermes | `skilled-loop hermes chat -q \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   117\t| Devin | `skilled-loop devin -- \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>\"` |\n   118\t\n   119\tThe CLI and wrapper place each path `!` in single quotes outside the seed's double quotes. For example, they print `skilled-loop claude \"[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff /tmp/han\"'!'\"doff.md\"`. Interactive Bash keeps that path intact when history expansion is on.\n   120\t\n   121\t---\n   122\t\n   123\t## 5. RECEIVING A HANDOFF\n   124\t\n   125\tA session seeded with `[session-relaunch] claim and continue handoff <path>` is on the other side of this protocol. It:\n   126\t\n   127\t1. Runs `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs claim <path> --session <session id>`, which moves the note `open -> claimed` and prints its body. Only Claude Code may omit `--session` and use `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. A runtime without a session-id variable generates an id with `uuidgen` and reuses it for the session.\n   128\t2. Reads the note's Goal, Done, Remaining work and In-flight state sections.\n   129\t3. Runs `/speckit:resume <spec_folder>` when the field contains a repo-relative packet path. When it is `none`, Gate 3 was answered D) Skip and the receiver does not ask it again. When it is empty, Gate 3 was never answered and the receiver asks it as usual.\n   130\t4. Continues the Remaining work.\n   131\t5. Runs `node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs complete <path>` when the handoff is fully absorbed.\n   132\t\n   133\tThe note's status moves only `open -> claimed -> done`. When this session prepares a successor hop, `prepare` marks every other note this session claimed as `done`, sets `completed_at` and adds `superseded_by` with the new note's basename. It leaves open notes, done notes, notes claimed by another session and the new note unchanged.\n   134\t\n   135\t---\n   136\t\n   137\t## 6. EXAMPLES\n   138\t\n   139\t**Example 1: inside the loop**\n   140\t\n   141\t```text\n   142\t/speckit:handoff\n   143\t```\n   144\t\n   145\tThe note is written and `prepare` exits `0`. On an automatic runtime, its arm event can qualify the record for relaunch when the session ends.\n   146\t\n   147\t**Example 2: outside the loop**\n   148\t\n   149\t```text\n   150\t/speckit:handoff\n   151\t```\n   152\t\n   153\t`prepare` exits `3` and the command shows the selected runtime's printed claim command so the operator can run the hop by hand.\n   154\t\n   155\t---\n   156\t\n   157\t## 7. RELATED COMMANDS\n   158\t\n   159\t- `/speckit:save`: used before the note on Claude when a spec packet is bound. Other runtimes use the continuity writer.\n   160\t- `/speckit:resume`: runs on the receiving side when the note names a `spec_folder`.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat -n .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md | sed -n '1,220p'","time":{"start":1792421935625,"end":1792421935640}},"id":"prt_154ac3926001V5D2KHHQLqcEmM","sessionID":"ses_eab5d5530ffemUeXMVtsM2xDB5","messageID":"msg_154ac247f001yufM05azF2EZC9"}}
