ession-relaunch-loop.md:27-85\",\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/tests/claude-adapters.test.cjs:220-260\",\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/tests/codex-adapters.test.cjs\",\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.test.ts:30-42,285-310\",\".opencode/plugins/tests/session-relaunch.test.cjs:35-65,220-250\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"Claude nudge\",\"Pi extension\",\"OpenCode plugin\",\"Codex nudge\",\"Hermes nudge\",\"prepare\"],\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"plannedNotePath builds the handoff note path but never creates the handoffs directory; only /speckit:handoff does.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:219-260\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\",\"id\":\"DS-001\",\"recommendation\":\"Create the handoffs directory with mode 0700 in plannedNotePath and add a clean-state test.\",\"scopeProof\":\"All five automatic adapters route through plannedNotePath; no mkdir exists in nudge or the adapters.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The automatic nudge names a note path in a directory it never creates\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"nudge note planner\",\"/speckit:handoff\",\"prepare pending record\",\"claim/complete lifecycle\"],\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"prepare overwrites the loop record and supersedeClaimed only closes claimed notes, while openNotePathFor returns the first open note in directory order.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs:418-427\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\",\"id\":\"DS-002\",\"recommendation\":\"Reuse or supersede the session's open note before a new record, and prefer the newest open note; add a two-invocation test.\",\"scopeProof\":\"The two planners disagree and no test covers two open notes for one session.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A second handoff can orphan the first open note and a later nudge can reuse the stale path\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"handoff note write\",\"claim/complete updates\",\"prepare read\",\"all five automatic runtimes\",\"/speckit:handoff\"],\"dimension\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"The handoffs directory is only joined, not created with a private mode, and writeHandoffUpdate preserves the note's existing mode.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/nudge.cjs:209-213\",\"findingClass\":\"class-of-bug\",\"id\":\"DS-003\",\"recommendation\":\"Create the handoffs directory 0700, pin notes 0600, stop preserving a permissive mode, and assert the modes in tests.\",\"scopeProof\":\"All handoff writers use the same directory and the same preserved mode; no note mode pin exists.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"Handoff notes inherit the default permissive directory and file modes\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"phase 007 closure\",\"benchmark run 10 outcomes\",\"future review provenance\"],\"claimAdjudication\":{\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The log may be intentionally local-only because the repository ignores *.log; rejected because the AC marks the log citations Met and the benchmark declares requireDurableEvidence true.\",\"claim\":\"Phase 007's acceptance criteria and benchmark report cite a live-run log that is absent from the repository and excluded by the .gitignore *.log rule.\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Searched the evidence and benchmark directories, the whole repository, and sibling worktrees for the filename; checked git ls-files and git check-ignore; read the benchmark outcome JSON, which repeats the path and hash without embedding the bytes.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"If the AC and benchmark are amended to cite the tracked panes and outcome JSON as the durable record and the log claim is removed, downgrade to P2.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/acceptance-criteria.md:59-61\",\"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/implementation-summary.md:71\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-10-19--manual-testing-playbook--session-relaunch-gate-exemptions/README.md:44-49\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/benchmark/reports/2026-10-19--manual-testing-playbook--session-relaunch-gate-exemptions/source.md:19\",\".gitignore:263\"],\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingId\":\"DS-004\"},\"confidence\":0.97,\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"AC-006 to AC-008 cite relaunch-run10.log by line; the evidence directory has only launch-commands and pane captures; git check-ignore reports .gitignore:263 *.log.\",\"file\":\"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/007-handoff-gate-exemptions/acceptance-criteria.md:59-61\",\"findingClass\":\"documentation-evidence-defect\",\"id\":\"DS-004\",\"recommendation\":\"Store the log under a non-ignored name or add a targeted negation, update every citation and hash, or amend the AC to cite the tracked panes and outcome JSON.\",\"scopeProof\":\"The three AC rows and the benchmark rows name the missing path; git check-ignore proves the named path is excluded.\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"Phase 007 cites a live-run log that is absent and permanently ignored by Git\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"parent closure metadata\",\"phase scope\",\"phase file map\",\"006-to-007 handoff verification\"],\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"The metadata and purpose say six, In Scope and Files to Change stop at 006, and the final handoff row is TBD while the phase map lists 007 complete.\",\"file\":\"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/spec.md:39,51,62-67,79-86,122\",\"findingClass\":\"documentation-drift\",\"id\":\"DS-005\",\"recommendation\":\"Say seven, add phase 007 to In Scope and Files to Change, and fill the 006-to-007 handoff row.\",\"scopeProof\":\"rg over the file shows the seven-row phase map and the six-child prose in the same document.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The parent specification still counts six children and leaves the 006-to-007 handoff row undefined\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"phase 006 scope\",\"phase 006 acceptance evidence\",\"parent 005-to-006 handoff\",\"phase 004 continuity pointer\"],\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"The scope and dependency cite ../review/review-report.md and an absolute /private/tmp table; the report is absent from review/ and exists only in review-archive/20261019T144809Z; AC-010 and AC-011 repeat the stale path.\",\"file\":\"specs/hooks/023-session-relaunch-loop/006-deep-review-2-remediation/spec.md:40,43\",\"findingClass\":\"documentation-evidence-defect\",\"id\":\"DS-006\",\"recommendation\":\"Repoint to the archived report, copy the verification table into the packet or cite the archived section, and update AC-010 and AC-011.\",\"scopeProof\":\"The review tree has no review-report.md; the archived report exists and the stale citations are listed by rg.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"Phase 006's review evidence cites an absent report path and an ephemeral temp table\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"/speckit:handoff\",\"operator status line\",\"hop-cap decline\",\"auto-compaction fallback message\"],\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"The CLI table and Step 5 say exit 3 means outside skilled-loop; prepare returns 3 inside the loop at the hop cap after printing the decline and manual command.\",\"file\":\".skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:33,105-107\",\"findingClass\":\"documentation-drift\",\"id\":\"DS-007\",\"recommendation\":\"Describe exit 3 as outside-loop or at the hop cap, distinguish the lines and log reasons, and add a command-doc example.\",\"scopeProof\":\"session-relaunch.cjs has two return-3 paths; the command document describes only the outside-loop path.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The handoff command documents exit 3 as outside-loop only, while the CLI also returns 3 at the hop cap\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"killer stale-lock takeover\",\"runtime state directory\",\"operator diagnostics\"],\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"removeStaleLock renames a non-file to .stale-<pid>-<uuid> then rmSync; sweepStaleTakeovers only matches the .takeover.stale- prefix.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/killer.cjs:234-242\",\"findingClass\":\"class-of-bug\",\"id\":\"DS-008\",\"recommendation\":\"Sweep lock .stale- backups by age under the takeover mutex, or move to a reaped temp name; add a leftover test.\",\"scopeProof\":\"The only cleanup prefix in the module is the takeover prefix; the normal-path stale-directory test does not cover a crash leftover.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A crash between the stale-lock rename and its removal leaves an unswept lock backup\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"wrapper should-relaunch\",\"nudge handoffPending\",\"armed record freshness\",\"clock-step recovery\"],\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"The age check only rejects positive ages; a negative now-minus-armedAt passes, so a backward clock step or future timestamp keeps the record fresh.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/lib/relaunch-core.cjs:403-417\",\"findingClass\":\"algorithmic\",\"id\":\"DS-009\",\"recommendation\":\"Reject nowMs < armedAtMs - allowedSkewMs as stale and add future-armedAt tests for the wrapper and handoffPending.\",\"scopeProof\":\"shouldRelaunch is the only freshness gate; the wrapper and nudge both delegate to it.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"shouldRelaunch treats a future armedAt as fresh instead of stale\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"Pi adapter\",\"OpenCode plugin\",\"Hermes bridge\",\"ENV-REFERENCE\",\"session-relaunch README\"],\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"Pi and OpenCode read SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER; Hermes reads HERMES_SPEC_FOLDER and passes payload.spec_folder; the environment reference lists no spec-folder variable.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/pi/session-relaunch.ts:338\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\",\"id\":\"DS-010\",\"recommendation\":\"Document both inputs in ENV-REFERENCE and the README, or unify on one variable and read it from Claude and Codex too.\",\"scopeProof\":\"rg finds the adapter reads and the goal-binding reference but no row in the environment reference.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The carried-packet environment inputs are undocumented and differ by runtime\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"Claude context nudge\",\"Codex shared adapter\",\"Claude test suite\",\"Codex test suite\",\"D3 packet carry\"],\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"evidence\":\"Claude and Codex read payload.spec_folder, but rg finds no spec_folder in their adapter test files; the Claude seed test is the only spec-folder case.\",\"file\":\".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/claude/context-nudge.mjs:121-123\",\"findingClass\":\"matrix/evidence\",\"id\":\"DS-011\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a nudge-payload case per adapter with spec_folder set, or remove the dead reads and document that only the model writes the field.\",\"scopeProof\":\"The two adapter files are the only automatic runtimes whose nudge field is untested; Pi and OpenCode set the variable in their suites and Hermes passes the payload field.\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The Claude and Codex nudge tests never cover a carried spec_folder\"}],\"findingsCount\":11,\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":2},\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":1,\"P2\":10},\"focus\":\"adapter payload parity and documentation inputs\",\"generation\":1,\"graphEvents\":[{\"id\":\"dim-parity-5\",\"kind\":\"DIMENSION\",\"label\":\"adapter parity\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"file-pi-5\",\"kind\":\"FILE\",\"label\":\"Pi session-relaunch.ts\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"file-test-5\",\"kind\":\"FILE\",\"label\":\"Claude adapter tests\",\"type\":\"node\"},{\"id\":\"finding-ds-010\",\"kind\":